    description: "Found by the 2026-11-07 docstring staleness audit (dev 4f2feb451b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11072026/review, verify and blind). Corpus impact not measured. _scan never checks result.returncode; empty stdout hits `if not stdout or stdout == \"null\": return []` (gitleaks.py:368-369), so sketch prints 'Secret scan complete' and the cache stores findings: []. Reproduced with a fake gitleaks (echo error >&2; exit 1) via GITLEAKS_PATH: scan_content_cached('aws_secret=AKIA...') gives []. Same failure the recent secret-scan fix targeted, by another route; contradicts the Unreleased changelog line 'A secret scan that did not run says so and is never cached as clean'. r22, v09."  # a24d
